Backport of duckdb/duckdb c43659e69ba: multi-file scans honor
explicit_cardinality, and estimate from file sizes when no file is opened at
bind.

In v2.0.0 read_parquet ignores explicit_cardinality, and a scan with schema=
opens no file at bind, so it is estimated at one row. pg_lake passes both for
every Iceberg scan, so its plans saw one row per data file.

Adapted to v2.0.0: the opened reader's row count still takes precedence over
the bound one.

